# Check out every text file with LF line endings, on every OS.
#
# Git for Windows defaults to core.autocrlf=true, which would otherwise
# check text files out with CRLF. Several specs compare committed files
# byte for byte with generated output (adapter-reference, feature
# vocabulary, the docs' embedded examples), and the .sh scripts fail in
# Git Bash with `$'\r': command not found`, so a CRLF checkout breaks
# `pnpm test:unit` on Windows. Pinning eol=lf makes a Windows clone
# identical to a macOS or Linux one.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary: never touched.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary

# Recorded network fixtures for the screenshot harness. Each file's sha256
# is recorded in fixtures/index.json and one of them (an AlphaFold CSV) is
# CRLF as served upstream, so they must be checked out byte for byte.
scripts/screenshots/fixtures/net/** -text

# A metrics export with mixed line endings, kept as downloaded.
docs/program/npm_downloads.csv -text
